-Gradient estimation via finite differences is a fundamental technique in volume rendering for computing surface normals from scalar fields [S2, unofficial]. The specific implementation of selecting between Central and Sobel modes is documented in community resources [S1, unofficial]. The theoretical basis for finite difference gradients is covered in standard volume rendering literature [S2, unofficial].
